    "content" : "(3.24) for every t ∈ [t0,T]. This proves (3.23) and, therefore, that F is compact by the Ascoli-Arzelà theorem. Finally, the set {z ∈ C0([t0,T];Rd) | z = θF(z)for some θ ∈ [0,1]} is bounded thanks to (3.21) and (3.22). According to Schaefer’s ﬁxed point theorem, F admits at least one ﬁxed point z ∈ C0([t0,T];Rd), i.e., z = F(z) = xuz."
